    {
      "id": "aa221518-3199-4852-b79e-716b6976e307",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -144,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 848,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## How This Workflow Works\n- The workflow starts automatically using a scheduled trigger configured in n8n.\n- Latest news articles are fetched from external news APIs in real time.\n- Raw API responses are cleaned and transformed into structured article objects for consistent processing.\n- AI-related filtering removes unrelated news articles and keeps only relevant technology and AI updates.\n- OpenAI analyzes every article individually and generates useful insights such as summaries, sentiment, categories, importance scores, and trend keywords.\n- Original article details and AI-generated insights are merged together into a single structured dataset.\n- Before storing data, the workflow checks whether the article already exists in the database to prevent duplicate records.\n- Stored articles are analyzed again to identify trending keywords and prepare a digest-ready payload.\n- OpenAI generates a professional executive AI news digest using the collected insights and trend analysis.\n- Finally, the workflow automatically sends the generated digest to Slack, allowing teams to stay updated with important AI industry developments daily.\n\n\n\n## Workflow Setup Steps\n\n- Create a scheduled trigger to automatically run the workflow at a fixed time every day.\nConfigure the news API request node to fetch the latest AI-related news articles from trusted news sources.\n- Normalize and process the fetched news data into a clean structured format for easier filtering and analysis.\n- Apply AI-related keyword filtering to keep only relevant articles focused on artificial intelligence, machine learning, automation, and emerging technologies.\n- Send filtered articles to OpenAI for summarization, sentiment detection, category classification, importance scoring, and trend keyword extraction.\n- Parse the AI response and merge it with the original article data to create a complete enriched dataset.\n- Validate duplicate articles using PostgreSQL queries before storing records into the database.\n- Generate trend analytics and prepare a structured payload containing summarized articles and trending topics.\n- Use OpenAI again to generate a professional executive-style daily AI news digest based on the processed data.\n- Automatically deliver the final digest to Slack for daily team updates and monitoring."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
